  "jobTitle": "Web developer and web everything ",
  "summary": "Hello, I would like to be your go to remote or part time web developer. I have been doing this a very long time and most recently have integrated AI on one website, and at the moment, have gotten good at using Authorize.net payment gateway and related skills.  I have been programming since before there was an internet.\n\nI have over 18 years computer programmer/ analyst and full stack web development experience,  plus recent junior level web3 developer skills but still learning web3.    I am very good at fixing problems with websites and javascript issues and figuring out issues and solving problems in general.     My first programming job doing RPG and AS400 was at a corporate headquarters of Ralph Lauren Polo Leathergoods division before the year 2000 and have had a bit of corporate experience so comfortable in that environment or remote either.  I live in Orange County.\n\nI have a lot of experience doing all kinds of backend projects and front-end developer gigs and mostly coding , not designing.    I feel that I have enough experience over several platforms, and the necessary skills to be able to handle any language, or platform readily and hit the ground running.   I have spent a great deal of time keeping my skills current including Node js and the new react Javascript and many others, so am really good at knowing which technologies to use for a project,  and also am able to wear multiple hats, and am not afraid of any platform or language, I am not set in my ways, willing to take advice and even do things the way you want me to .  Have great attitude working with others and working alone.  I don't hide it if there's a problem or issue.   I am willing to start out at a junior level to prove myself or can walk into a regular dev position with no fear.  \n\nLooking for a good position I can make my greatest accomplishments yet at.    And somewhere I can stay for a long time and possibly accrue some retirement savings.  I want to be your go to guy getting stuff done for you and reliable always there for you.\n\nRecent: learning tensorflow.js and working on training a model for AI project. Three js.   Data scraping with node.js\n\nMost recently: wrote a complete ticketing system for a music club including webhook for Authorize.net.   Also a fixityerself type website to fix home appliances aimed at older people who don't like AI, it does use AI, but makes it into a readable format for older people who don't like Ai responses.  Also steady stream of regular websites, and maintenance for people on all things computer.",
